\fs20\fsmilli10462 In the second expertise layer, the focus shifts to AI's role in enhancing ID, particularly\
in creating learning activities. As Instructional Designers craft educational activities to\
efficiently and precisely deliver knowledge, AI emerges as a vital ally.\
It streamlines the creation of educational artifacts and transforms training content,\
aligning it with learning objectives and learner needs. AI's adaptability ensures more\
personalized, engaging, and effective learning experiences, revolutionizing instruction-\
al material design and development.\

\fs31\fsmilli15693 2.1\
AI can produce a very rich variety of educational artifacts\

\fs20\fsmilli10462 Educational artifacts are essential, tangi-\
ble, physical, or digital materials crafted or\
selected by Instructional Designers to aid\
learning. These can range from flashcards\
to glossaries and presentations. Crafting\
these artifacts is a creative and demand-\
ing task. AI drastically enhances this pro-\
cess by instantly creating or transforming\
artifacts with unparalleled innovation and\
efficiency.\
IDs can leverage AI to produce con-\
tent-specific artifacts by providing AI-spe-\
cific data from various sources (e.g., web-\
sites, files, etc) as input, revolutionizing\
instructional design with tailored precision.\
The list of educational artifacts that AI\
can generate effectively is almost end-\
less. Here is a simple prompt that you can\
tailor to meet your audience, topic, and\
learning objectives. We are certain that\
the results will most certainly amaze you!\

\fs19\fsmilli9590 Develop a [type of educational artifact]: Flash Card Questions/ Timelines/ ill-in-the-\
blank-Questions/Assignments/Journal Prompt Questions/Glossary/Slides/Video Script/\
Audio Script/Dilemma/Case Study/Role-playing scenarios/Storyboard/Stories/Self-\
Assessment Checklists/ Evaluation matrices-rubrics/Peer Review/Images that engages\
[target audience] and meets [learning objectives].
