\fs20\fsmilli10462 The fourth layer of expertise emphasizes the significance of crafting engineered\
prompts for AI to generate instructional plans. These plans provide a clear roadmap,\
detailing course outlines, learning objectives, and audience-specific needs. In this\
section, we analyze how Instructional Designers can leverage AI in four areas essen-\
tial for building stellar instructional plans.\

\fs31\fsmilli15693 4.1\
AI can help you understand your Learners\

\fs20\fsmilli10462 Creating instructional plans without\
understanding learners is like planning a\
trip without knowing the travelers\'92 pref-\
erences. Despite its organization, it lacks\
purpose and relevance. This analogy un-\
derscores the importance of aligning IDs\
with the specific needs of primary learn-\
ers from diverse domains.\
In ID, learners are most likely profession-\
als. Thus, clearly understanding learners'\
backgrounds and preferences is critical.\
We offer five categories of learner-cen-\
tric prompting and examples of prompts\
that can facilitate your design of tailored\
educational experiences:\

\fs22\fsmilli11334 Learning characteristics Learner's profile exploration\

