\fs20\fsmilli10462 A theory-driven approach in ID ensures\
the creation of academically robust and\
impactful educational materials. AI sig-\
nificantly aids in this process, allowing\
designers to leverage theory-informed\
outcomes without mastering every in-\
structional theory.\
Instructional Designers need to clarify\
how Learning Theories (e.g., Behaviorism,\
Constructivism, Cognitivism, Connectiv-\
ism) lay the foundational understanding\
of how learning occurs, framing the ID\
Models, which provide structured meth-\
odologies for crafting educational expe-\
riences as well as the ID Principles, which\
deliver practical, actionable guidelines.\
Among the most influencing ID Models\
are the ADDIE model, Bloom\'92s Taxonomy,\
SMART Goals, Kirkpatrick's Four Levels\
of Evaluation, Successive Approximation\
Model (SAM), Action Mapping, Kolb\'92s\
experiential learning, and Problem-based\
learning. Moreover, among the most\
influencing ID principles are Gagne\'92s nine\
events of instruction and Merrill\'92s Princi-\
ples of Instruction.\

\fs22\fsmilli11334 Let\'92s see a prompt example that could be of use:\

\fs19\fsmilli9590 Act as [role and expertise]. You need to develop [syllabus/course outline, etc.] for your\
upcoming course on [topic] addressed to [my audience]. Base your work on the ADDIE\
learning model/SAM/Problem-based learning/Experiential learning.
